`Dana: electrical work outside the integral electrical system` MEANS `fixture: limits of the item set in the situation` (`fixture: the work of` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `holding` (LIST `Dana: a grade 1 licence granted on 1 February 2029`) `on` (YMD 2030 4 1) `on the system` `R134a, 10 kW` `amounting to` `A.1(12) electrical work in the integral electrical system only`) `to` `fixture: facts with neither limit satisfied`
#ASSERT `int — the act of the situation is work on a cooling system` `Dana: electrical work in the integral electrical system on 1 April 2030, licence in force`
#ASSERT `int — the licensee of the situation is treated as a service electrician` `Dana: electrical work in the integral electrical system on 1 April 2030, licence in force`
#ASSERT `int — the licensee of the situation may do the electrical work under section 61` `Dana: electrical work in the integral electrical system on 1 April 2030, licence in force`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the licensee of the situation is treated as a service electrician` `Dana: the same electrical work, licence lapsed`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the licensee of the situation may do the electrical work under section 61` `Dana: the same electrical work, licence lapsed`
-- Outside the integral electrical system the act is not "work on a cooling system" (s.2, First Schedule item A12), so on the integrated wiring neither section lets the licensee do it.
#ASSERT NOT `int — the act of the situation is work on a cooling system` `Dana: electrical work outside the integral electrical system`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the licensee of the situation is treated as a service electrician` `Dana: electrical work outside the integral electrical system`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the licensee of the situation may do the electrical work under section 61` `Dana: electrical work outside the integral electrical system`

§§ `S18. An exemption order and the ordering of the reasons s.3(a) does not apply (groups 1, 4, 7)`

#ASSERT `int — the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an exemption` `with the Minister's satisfaction being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order after` `fixture: a consultation on an exemption at a meeting without a quorum` `with the Minister's satisfaction being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an exemption` `with the Minister's satisfaction being` FALSE
-- A subcommittee cannot give the Council's advice on function (1): only on function (3) (group 4, s.26(b)).
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order after` (`int — a consultation on an exemption whose advice came from` (`a subcommittee that advises the Council` WITH `the Council delegated its powers in the function to the subcommittee` IS TRUE, `the subcommittee proceeded as the procedure fixed by the Council requires` IS JUST TRUE)) `with the Minister's satisfaction being` TRUE
`Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW, 1 April 2030, in an exempted class` MEANS `fixture: the system exempted by an order in the situation` (`fixture: the work of` `fixture: Noa, an individual` `holding` EMPTY `on` (YMD 2030 4 1) `on the system` `R134a, 10 kW` `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`)
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` `Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW, 1 April 2030, in an exempted class` EQUALS `section 3(a) does not apply: the system is of a class the Minister exempted by order under section 3(b)`
#ASSERT `int — the person may do the work of` `Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW, 1 April 2030, in an exempted class`
-- Before the Law has commenced for paragraph (2) systems (16.1.2027) the first reason is that it has not commenced.
`Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW, 1 June 2026, in an exempted class` MEANS `fixture: the system exempted by an order in the situation` (`fixture: the work of` `fixture: Noa, an individual` `holding` EMPTY `on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `on the system` `R134a, 10 kW` `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`)
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` `Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW, 1 June 2026, in an exempted class` EQUALS `section 3(a) does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for work on the system`
-- Without the exemption, unlicensed work on 1.4.2030 is forbidden: item (1).
`Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW, 1 April 2030` MEANS `fixture: the work of` `fixture: Noa, an individual` `holding` EMPTY `on` (YMD 2030 4 1) `on the system` `R134a, 10 kW` `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` `Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW, 1 April 2030` EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all`

§§ `S08 (continued). The inspector's powers where the Law has not yet commenced for the work supervised (groups 5, 7)`

-- Group 5 gates an inspector's powers on a field of the occasion; the integration fills it from group 7.  An R134a system is reached by the Law from 16.1.2027: on 1.6.2026 the inspector may not use the power to require a document, on 1.4.2030 he may.
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector may use the power` (`int — the inspector's occasion with the commencement of the Law for` `R134a, 10 kW` `on the day` (YMD 2026 6 1) `set in` `an inspector who is fully equipped`) `require information or a document`
#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` (`int — the inspector's occasion with the commencement of the Law for` `R134a, 10 kW` `on the day` (YMD 2030 4 1) `set in` `an inspector who is fully equipped`) `require information or a document`
-- For propane (paragraph (1), from 16.7.2025) the same inspector may use it on 1.6.2026.
#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` (`int — the inspector's occasion with the commencement of the Law for` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "290") `on the day` (YMD 2026 6 1) `set in` `an inspector who is fully equipped`) `require information or a document`

§§ `Edges: the day paragraph (2) of s.63(a) begins, and a corporation with no licence`

-- Unlicensed work on a 10 kW R134a system: on 15.1.2027 the Law has not commenced for it; on 16.1.2027 (18 months after 16.7.2025) it has, and the work is forbidden, item (1).
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Situation of one piece of work`
`Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW R134a on` day MEANS `fixture: the work of` `fixture: Noa, an individual` `holding` EMPTY `on` day `on the system` `R134a, 10 kW` `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` (`Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW R134a on` (YMD 2027 1 15)) EQUALS `section 3(a) does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for work on the system`
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` (`Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW R134a on` (YMD 2027 1 16)) EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all`
-- A corporation that works with no licence at all commits item (1), whose corporation column is a dash: the violation is found, and its sanction is a refusal (never zero, never the individual's 20,000).
`Kar-Kor: unlicensed work on 10 kW on 1 April 2030` MEANS `fixture: the work of` `fixture: Kar-Kor Ltd, a corporation` `holding` EMPTY `on` (YMD 2030 4 1) `on the system` `R134a, 10 kW` `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`
#ASSERT `int — the violation committed under section 3(a) by` `Kar-Kor: unlicensed work on 10 kW on 1 April 2030` `with the reference` "karkor-unlicensed" EQUALS JUST (Violation WITH `the violator` IS `fixture: Kar-Kor Ltd, a corporation`, `the listed violation` IS `work with no licence at all`, `reference for the act` IS "karkor-unlicensed", `date of the act` IS YMD 2030 4 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — the sanction for the work of` `Kar-Kor: unlicensed work on 10 kW on 1 April 2030` `with the reference` "karkor-unlicensed" `priced from` `the pricing updated on 15 June 2030` `with the commencement` `the section 46 hypothesis`

§§ `S21. From unlicensed work to the appeal, day by day (groups 1, 6, 7)`

-- Written from the Hebrew text before it was run (expectations.md, S21).  Noa, an individual with no licence, works on a 10 kW R134a system on 1 April 2030.
-- Chapter 6 has commenced (the hypothetical regulation of s.46 is in force and 18 months have passed), so item (1) prices the work: NIS 20,000 for an individual, times 102/100 for the 1.1.2026 update, NIS 20,400.
-- The Commissioner delivers a complete notice of intention on Saturday 15 June 2030 (no day of rest is taken: the calendar is empty).
-- Every period is "30 days from" or "45 days from" a day, so IL s.10(a) leaves the day of delivery out and the last day is the day that many days later,
-- and (the convention the register records as R2) an act on the day of delivery itself is within the period.
-- Representations: 30 days from 15.6.2030 end on 15.7.2030 (June has 30 days: 15 days to 30.6, 15 more to 15.7).
-- A violator who stays silent: the notice is treated as a payment demand delivered on that last day, 15.7.2030 (s.44(d)).
-- Payment: 30 days from 15.7.2030 end on 14.8.2030 (16 days to 31.7, 14 more).
-- Appeal: 45 days from the day notice of the decision counts as delivered, 15.7.2030, end on 29.8.2030 (16 days to 31.7, 29 more).

`S21: the Commissioner's notice of 15 June 2030` MEANS `Notice of intention` WITH
    `delivered on` IS YMD 2030 6 15
    `in writing` IS TRUE
    `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS TRUE
    `states the amount of the sanction` IS TRUE
    `the period for payment the notice states, in days` IS JUST 30
    `states the violator's right to make representations under section 43` IS TRUE
    `states that the notice will be treated as a payment demand if the right is not used` IS TRUE
    `states the power to add for a continuing or repeat violation and the rate of the addition` IS TRUE
    `states the intention to publish the violator's name` IS FALSE
`S21: no extension granted` MEANS NOTHING

-- The violation and its price.
#ASSERT `int — the sanction for the work of` (`Noa: unlicensed work on 10 kW R134a on` (YMD 2030 4 1)) `with the reference` "noa-s21" `priced from` `the pricing updated on 15 June 2030` `with the commencement` `the section 46 hypothesis` EQUALS `the sanction is` 20400
-- The window for representations.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` `S21: the Commissioner's notice of 15 June 2030` `S21: no extension granted` `fixture: no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2030 7 15
#ASSERT `s 43 — the day` (YMD 2030 6 15) `is within the period for representations of` `S21: the Commissioner's notice of 15 June 2030` `S21: no extension granted` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT `s 43 — the day` (YMD 2030 7 15) `is within the period for representations of` `S21: the Commissioner's notice of 15 June 2030` `S21: no extension granted` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 43 — the day` (YMD 2030 7 16) `is within the period for representations of` `S21: the Commissioner's notice of 15 June 2030` `S21: no extension granted` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
-- Silence: the notice is treated as a payment demand delivered on 15.7.2030.
#ASSERT `s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` `S21: the Commissioner's notice of 15 June 2030` `S21: no extension granted` `fixture: no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2030 7 15
-- Payment: 30 days from that demand.
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` (YMD 2030 7 15) `fixture: no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2030 8 14
#ASSERT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2030 8 14) `is within the period for payment that runs from` (YMD 2030 7 15) `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2030 8 15) `is within the period for payment that runs from` (YMD 2030 7 15) `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
-- Appeal: the day notice of the decision counts as delivered to a violator who made no representations is the demand's day, and 45 days from it end on 29.8.2030.
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the day notice of the decision counts as delivered to a violator who made no representations` `S21: the Commissioner's notice of 15 June 2030` `S21: no extension granted` `fixture: no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2030 7 15
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2030 7 15) `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2030 8 29
-- An appeal on the day the notice of the decision counts as delivered (15.7.2030) is within the 45 days, as an act on the day of delivery is under s.43, s.48 and s.53(a).
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2030 7 15) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2030 7 15) `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2030 8 29) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2030 7 15) `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2030 8 30) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2030 7 15) `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
